jobs.description:
We’re looking for a reach truck operator who is skilled at driving this type of equipment for a dynamic organization in the Echt region. In this role, you’ll be responsible for handling incoming and outgoing goods using a reach truck. Does working in a clean, well-organized facility energize you? This permanent position offers you job security on the day shift!

Duties:

- Placing pallets of products on shelves using a single-deep or double-deep reach truck;
- Picking orders; 
- Assisting with loading containers; 
- Supporting all logistical tasks as they arise.

You’ll spend most of your time operating the reach truck, so it’s important that you have experience with this type of logistics vehicle. Do you see yourself in this role? Don’t hesitate—read on!

This is a day shift position from 6:00 AM to 3:00 PM, Monday through Friday. 

- Experience operating a reach truck and a certificate demonstrating that you possess the qualities of a good reach truck operator;
- You speak Dutch, English, or German.

Are you an avid cleaner or cleaner? Do you want to make sure that vacationing guests can start their vacation with a good feeling? Then read on quickly! 

We are looking for part-time cleaning employees for vacation park de Leistert in Roggel. Mondays and Fridays are the so-called changeover days when new guests arrive at the cottage. On these days it is important that the bungalows and vacation homes are cleaned properly. You do this with a whole team of enthusiastic and motivated cleaners. Together you make sure that everything looks spic and span. 

Tasks you will perform include:

- Making beds;
- Cleaning the kitchen, bathroom, bedroom and living room;
- Dusting and mopping everything; 
- Identifying defects and passing them on to the right people so that they can be repaired in a timely manner.

The work takes place on Mondays and Fridays between 9 a.m. and 3 p.m. Would you like to work more? Please let us know so we can discuss the possibilities! 

- You are a motivated cleaner who knows how to get things done;
- You speak the Dutch, English or German language;
- It is no problem to come to the location in Roggel (public transport is also possible); 
- You are available at least on Mondays and Fridays.

In the vacation periods it is always extra busy, it is important that you are flexible in these periods!

- Venlo - 40 uur - € 18,70 per uur 
Are you looking for a challenging position as a Reachstacker Driver in Venlo? Do you enjoy working with heavy equipment and keeping a cool head in a dynamic terminal environment? At the terminal in Greenport Venlo, containers from sea, road, and rail come together. You ensure that everything is handled safely, efficiently, and on time. No container is too heavy, and no schedule is too tight. Thanks to your experience and expertise, the terminal keeps moving day and night 
What do we offer? 
• An hourly wage of €18,70, including shift allowances; 
• Working in a 2-shift system between 06:00 and 00:00; 
• Working one Saturday every four weeks, compensated as time off in lieu; 
• A solid pension scheme; 
• Full travel allowance of €0.23 per kilometre; 
• The opportunity to work with modern and well-maintained equipment; 
• Career development opportunities within a growing family-owned company; 
• A varied position in a professional terminal environment. 
What will you do? - Load and unload containers from trucks and rail wagons; - Move and correctly position containers in the stack using the reachstacker; - Occasionally operate the terminal tractor to move trailers; - Coordinate with planning, gate operations, and colleagues on the terminal; - Monitor safety, quality, and efficiency at all times; - Respond quickly to changes in the planning; - Work in a 2-shift schedule. 
What do you bring? - Experience as a Reachstacker Driver is a strong advantage; - No reachstacker experience yet, but affinity with logistics and experience operating a forklift or reach truck? We also encourage you to apply; - You take responsibility for your work and your machine; - You remain calm and flexible when situations change; - You have a good command of Dutch or, at the very least, good English communication skills; - You are willing to work in shifts; - Safety is always your top priority. 
